WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.700
It's time for us to talk about two
basic types of neurotransmission:

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.100
excitation and inhibition.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.320
Excitation and Inhibition require
a delicate and orchestrated balance

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.740
between pre- and postsynaptic processes.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.300
Signal transmission is
mediated by neurotransmitters

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.420
that are released presynaptically
AND by a large complexity

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.400
of postsynaptic mechanisms
and signalling pathways.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.650
The processes of
excitation and inhibition

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.030
occur because this wild
assortment of mechanisms

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.900
mediate postsynaptic potentials.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.640
Presynaptically, the cast of
characters is quite simple.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.270
We will see, for example, that fast
excitatory postsynaptic potentials are

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.800
mediated primarily by
cation-selective ion

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.520
channels in the postsynaptic neuron,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.640
alongside a host of other complex and
diverse postsynaptic players involved

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.470
in signalling pathways.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:54.300
Comparatively, the presynaptic
terminal is less of a party.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.269
Back in the postsynaptic terminal,
fast inhibitory postsynaptic potentials

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:07.860
are mediated primarily by
anion-selective ion channels.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.470
However, our simple, quiet
little neurotransmitters,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.250
waiting in the presynaptic terminal
for their action potential,

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.600
are absolutely necessary to
trigger postsynaptic mechanisms.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.490
What's so remarkable is the fact
that the delicate excitation-inhibition

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:24.690
balance throughout the brain can
be achieved with just a handful

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.950
of different types of
neurotransmitters and ions.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:39.190
For example, metabotropic receptors
like GPCRs will sense a neurotransmitter

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.010
and activate specific
signal transduction pathways

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:48.350
that ultimately change ion permeability
and other processes inside the cell.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.250
Other postsynaptic players,
like AMPA and NMDA receptors,

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.870
which mediate excitatory
communication and synaptic plasticity

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:59.790
in the central nervous system, are
permeable to many types of ions.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:08.040
The party is happening postsynaptically!

